Current production stack
========================

Adaptive speculative decoding
-----------------------------
Aiden Le (aidendle94) and local-inference-lab developed the acceptance-length
adaptive speculative-decoding foundation used here. This repository
forward-ports that work to the pinned DCP scheduler and modifies it with a
2/4/5 depth ladder, a k=2 floor, short k4/k5 probes, marginal per-position
decisions, multi-depth CUDA-graph coverage, and structured MTP telemetry.
The exact modifications are documented in CHANGES.md and adaptive-mtp/README.md.

Distributed context parallelism and sparse attention
----------------------------------------------------
The DCP serving base and GLM draft path derive from Apache-2.0 vLLM work by
m9e / voipmonitor and the broader vLLM community. The two PR #72 patches in
patches/ are preserved as third-party patches. Zatz demonstrated the 655k GB10
configuration that this repository independently reproduced and packaged.

The portable sm12x sparse-MLA and DeepGEMM-fallback kernel lineage is credited
to jasl and the vLLM project. The legacy kernels/ tree contains modified
Apache-2.0 vLLM source; its original SPDX and copyright headers are retained.
This repository's modifications include the GLM V3.2 adapter, int64 overflow
and bounds fixes, the fused gather/dequantize/attention prefill path, and the
32-to-16 decode-head padding follow-up. The earlier 64-to-32 head-padding fix
is credited to back199640. The fused indexer Q/RoPE quantization code is
upstream vLLM work by yewentao256 and is not original to this repository.

Vision integration
------------------
The local GLM-5V wrapper specializes Apache-2.0 vLLM Kimi multimodal code for
GlmMoeDsa and preserves QuantTrio's tensor and quantization layout. Baseten's
GLM-5.2-Vision-NVFP4 supplied the MIT-licensed projector, the frozen MoonViT
packaging, configuration/processing reference, and chat template. MoonViT and
the Kimi multimodal lineage are credited to Moonshot AI under its upstream
Modified MIT terms.

